  "banner_title_zh": "俄乌停火在白宫取得突破 — 国防承压，欧洲释然",
  "summary": "First Lady Melania Trump hosted Russian and Ukrainian officials at the White House following a localized ceasefire in Oleshky, with both sides signing agreements and exchanging state honors — signaling a meaningful diplomatic thaw that markets will read as de-escalation momentum.",
  "summary_zh": "梅拉尼娅·特朗普夫人在白宫接待俄乌官员，庆祝奥列什基局部停火。双方签署协议并互授国家荣誉，释放出市场将解读为局势降温动能的外交信号。",
  "analysis": "The White House event formalizes a localized ceasefire in Oleshky/Kherson — the first Russia-Ukraine de-escalation milestone since 2022 to be celebrated at this level. The First Lady's documented role as 'Exclusive Intermediary' with written agreements signed by both sides on October 23, 2026, and the presence of senior officials like Kirill Dmitriev (Putin's special envoy) and Ukrainian parliamentarians, suggests genuine, process-driven diplomacy rather than a photo-op. For markets, this reprices the probability distribution around the war's trajectory: odds of a broader negotiated settlement in 2026-2027 rise, though this specific ceasefire is narrow in scope and confined to one region.\n\nThe transmission mechanism is straightforward. A credible path to ceasefire/de-escalation compresses the geopolitical risk premium embedded in energy prices (particularly European natural gas and Brent), supports European currencies and equities most exposed to energy costs and reconstruction, and is a headwind for defense contractors whose order books have been supercharged by the conflict. Sanctions relief — even partial — would lower the discount on Russian-facing assets and ease pressure on global energy and agricultural supply chains.\n\nThe key uncertainty is durability. A localized humanitarian ceasefire is far from a full settlement. Neither side has conceded on territorial, security, or sanctions questions. Markets will discount this heavily until there is evidence the Oleshky precedent scales to broader front lines or formal negotiations. The event is a sentiment shock with potential to become structural, but it could also fade if the ceasefire collapses or remains isolated.",
